{
    "title": "Director Remuneration and Stakeholders Relationship Committee Report",
    "summary": "The page details remuneration for part-time official and independent directors, including sitting fees for board and committee meetings, and lists fees paid to seven independent directors totaling ₹33,85,000. It states no commission, stock options, or pecuniary relationships exist. It covers the Stakeholders Relationship Committee's FY 2024-25 composition, compliance with regulations, noting non-compliance from February 7, 2025, due to insufficient independent directors. It mentions the committee's chairman attended the 70th AGM, the committee met once, and lists its functions: resolving grievances, reviewing voting rights, service standards, and reducing unclaimed dividends. It also provides attendance details for the meeting on January 30, 2025, and positions as of March 31, 2025.",
}

{
    "title": "Director Non-Disqualification and Code Compliance Declarations",
    "summary": "The page contains two compliance sections from Bharat Electronics Limited's Integrated Annual Report 2024-25. First, a Certificate of Non-Disqualification of Directors certifies that none of the 16 listed directors were debarred or disqualified by SEBI, MCA, or other authorities for FY ending 31 March 2025, providing director details, DINs, designations, and appointment/cessation dates. Second, a Declaration of Compliance with the Code of Business Conduct and Ethics states that all Board Members and Senior Management Personnel affirmed compliance with the Code for the year ended 31 March 2025, pursuant to SEBI LODR and DPE guidelines. Both are signed by authorized persons with dates and locations.",
}
